{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27281193","formula":"C₁₂H₁₀O₇","hill":"C12H10O7","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":12.0,"H":10.0,"O":7.0},"names":{"en":"Echinochrome A"},"descriptions":{"en":"Echinochrome A (7-ethyl-2,3,5,6,8-pentahydroxy-1,4-naphthoquinone) is a polyhydroxylated 1,4-naphthoquinone, a type of pigments commonly found in sea urchin shell (\"test\"), spine, gonads, coelomic fluid, and eggs, of sea urchin. These types of pigments are commonly known as spinochromes and are natural marine phenolic compounds with potential pharmacological effects and modes of action. First extracted from the sea urchin Scaphechinus mirabilis, it is the active substance of histochrome and Echino-A. Histochrome is used for ophthalmic diseases and ischemic heart disease."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":135457951,"mass":266.2,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCC1=C(C2=C(C(=C1O)O)C(=O)C(=C(C2=O)O)O)O","inchikey":"DNRFNICCPHGYAX-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"6-ethyl-2,3,5,7,8-pentahydroxynaphthalene-1,4-dione","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"135457951","atoms":29,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-3.749,"y":-1.102,"z":0.451,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.009,"y":-0.728,"z":-0.824,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.663,"y":-0.102,"z":-0.533,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.516,"y":-0.911,"z":-0.433,"el":"C"},{"x":0.753,"y":-0.355,"z":-0.183,"el":"C"},{"x":0.892,"y":1.024,"z":-0.022,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.244,"y":1.841,"z":-0.101,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.507,"y":1.281,"z":-0.345,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.572,"y":2.141,"z":-0.396,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.177,"y":3.204,"z":0.065,"el":"O"},{"x":2.223,"y":1.615,"z":0.238,"el":"C"},{"x":2.329,"y":2.83,"z":0.379,"el":"O"},{"x":3.399,"y":0.707,"z":0.321,"el":"C"},{"x":3.257,"y":-0.611,"z":0.166,"el":"C"},{"x":1.937,"y":-1.225,"z":-0.092,"el":"C"},{"x":1.858,"y":-2.445,"z":-0.224,"el":"O"},